# Cloudflare Pages routing for the civfix community web static export.
#
# Next STATIC EXPORT (output: "export", trailingSlash: true): every route is a directory with an
# index.html in out/. The dynamic DETAIL routes are catch-alls (app/<route>/[...id]/page.tsx) whose
# generateStaticParams emit a single placeholder shell at out/<route>/_/index.html; the real id is
# read from the live URL at runtime (src/hooks/use-detail-id.ts). Cloudflare cannot know real ids,
# so it must serve that placeholder shell for every /<route>/<id> deep link with a 200 (rewrite,
# not redirect) so the SPA boots and resolves the id client-side.
#
# Two Cloudflare Pages behaviors shape these rules. BOTH were verified against `wrangler pages dev`
# (the real Pages routing engine), because the official docs leave them unspecified:
#
#  1. A _redirects rule is followed even when a static asset matches the request, AND the `*` splat
#     also matches the EMPTY remainder. So `/cleanups/* ... 200` matches the bare `/cleanups/` too
#     and would shadow the real browse page exported at out/cleanups/index.html (serving the empty
#     detail shell instead of the listing).
#     => We add higher-priority protective rules for the colliding browse routes (cleanups, people,
#        messages). Cloudflare evaluates static (splat-free) rules before splat rules, so they win.
#
#  2. Cloudflare IGNORES any redirect whose destination is canonicalized by stripping `/index.html`
#     (it reports "infinite loop detected" and drops the rule). So a destination must be a DIRECTORY
#     ( /foo/ ), never /foo/index.html. The detail shells already live at the directory
#     out/<route>/_/, so the deep-link rules target /<route>/_/ directly. The browse pages live at
#     out/<route>/index.html, which we cannot point at; a post-build step
#     (scripts/cf-pages-postbuild.mjs) copies each browse page to out/__spa/<route>/index.html so the
#     protective rule can target the directory /__spa/<route>/.
#
# /pin has no browse page, so it needs no protective rule. This file is copied into out/_redirects by
# the export; Cloudflare consumes it at deploy time (it is not served as an asset). After deploying,
# verify: curl -sI https://<host>/cleanups/ (browse) and curl -sI https://<host>/cleanups/<id>/ (detail).

# 1) Protect the real browse/index pages (served from their /__spa/<route>/ copy; see note 2 above).
/cleanups/   /__spa/cleanups/   200
/people/     /__spa/people/     200
/messages/   /__spa/messages/   200
/compose/    /__spa/compose/    200

# 2) SPA fallback for dynamic detail deep links (directory-form destination = no infinite-loop).
# /groups and /channels (Telegram-style chat) have no browse page - like /pin - so they need only the
# fallback rule, no protective /__spa/ rule. They cover /groups/new, /groups/<id>/info and
# /channels/new; a channel CONVERSATION rides the group rails as /messages/group/<id>, so it is served
# by the /messages/* rule below. Pinned-messages (/messages/pins/...) is also under /messages/*.
/pin/*        /pin/_/        200
/cleanups/*   /cleanups/_/   200
/people/*     /people/_/     200
/messages/*   /messages/_/   200
/groups/*     /groups/_/     200
/channels/*   /channels/_/   200
/post/*       /post/_/       200
/compose/*    /compose/_/    200

# /leaderboard/<geoid> (the jurisdiction service-hours leaderboard) and /service-record/<code> (the
# PUBLIC certificate verification page a school registrar lands on from a printed transcript). Like /pin,
# /groups and /channels, NEITHER has a browse page exported at out/<route>/index.html, so neither needs a
# protective /__spa/ rule: the collision detector in scripts/cf-pages-postbuild.mjs never fires for them.
# (That detector EXITS 1 when a protective rule IS required and missing, so a future browse page added
# under either prefix breaks the build rather than silently shadowing itself in production.)
/leaderboard/*      /leaderboard/_/      200
/service-record/*   /service-record/_/   200

# 3) Host-platform routes. Both are catch-all placeholder shells with NO browse page at
# out/<route>/index.html, so (like /pin, /groups and /channels) neither needs a protective /__spa/
# rule: the collision detector in scripts/cf-pages-postbuild.mjs never fires for them, and its
# SPA-fallback completeness check proves the reverse (every emitted /_/ shell HAS a rule here).
#
#   /manage/*     the host console (src/app/manage/[...path]), event id in the path
#   /e/*          the public signup page (src/app/e/[...slug]); ALSO routed through
#                 functions/e/[[path]].ts for per-event link previews, hence the _routes.json include
#
# /unsubscribe deliberately has NO rule: it is a STATIC page (out/unsubscribe/index.html) whose token
# rides in the query string, so a splat rule here would shadow the page it points at and Cloudflare
# would drop it as an infinite loop.
/manage/*     /manage/_/     200
/e/*          /e/_/          200

# /orgs/<slug> is the PUBLIC organization page (src/app/orgs/[...slug]); the in-app nav also maps
# /orgs/<slug> to the shared org panel, so a cold load boots this standalone shell and a warm click
# stays inside the app. No browse page, so no protective rule; routed through functions/orgs/[[path]].ts
# for per-organization link previews, hence the _routes.json include.
/orgs/*       /orgs/_/       200
